	<h3>Windows (64-bit)</h3>
	<pre class="cmd">irm https://cone.jondgoodwin.com/install.ps1 | iex</pre>
	<p>The script downloads the zip below, checks its SHA-256, unpacks it into
	<code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Cone</code> and puts it on your user PATH. It needs no administrator rights.
	Python is included (Congo runs on Microsoft's embeddable Python), so there is nothing to install for that.</p>
	<table class="files">
	<tr><td>File</td><td><a href="downloads/@HASH8@/@WIN_FILE@">@WIN_FILE@</a> (@WIN_SIZE@)</td></tr>
	<tr><td>SHA-256</td><td><code class="hash">@WIN_SHA256@</code></td></tr>
	</table>
	<p><b>You need</b> Windows 10 or 11 and
	<a href="https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/">Microsoft's C++ Build Tools</a>
	(Build Tools for Visual Studio 2022, workload "Desktop development with C++"), because Congo links programs
	with Microsoft's linker. The installer checks for them and prints how to get them if they are missing.
	<a href="https://git-scm.com/downloads">Git</a> must be on your PATH for Congo to fetch packages by name.</p>

